**Baseline renal function** – PAT‑009 entered the admission with chronic kidney disease (baseline creatinine 1.3 mg/dL, eGFR ≈ 40 mL/min/1.73 m²)【HO-08, 3.5】.  

**Medication list at the time of the error** – The patient was already receiving lisinopril (ACE‑inhibitor) and furosemide (loop diuretic). An ibuprofen prescription (600 mg TID) was added on 2026‑03‑05【HO-08, 3.5】.  

**Drug‑interaction / renal‑risk assessment** – The MediCore reconciliation protocol (PRO‑001) requires that each drug pair be checked against the interaction database (MP‑06) and that every drug be checked against kidney function (MP‑07)【DG-08, 5.2】. An NSAID in a patient with eGFR < 60 mL/min/1.73 m², especially when combined with an ACE‑inhibitor, is a known precipitant of AKI;
